STABLE
------
=== Adopt the `stable` pseudo-version between releases

=== Add `0.2.0--0.2.1` update script
`ALTER EXTENSION trunklet UPDATE` now works from 0.2.0. Previously there was no update path from 0.2.0.
Updated installs now also match a fresh install: the `language__get()` debug message that a fresh 0.3.3 install has is added by `0.3.3--stable` and was retroactively added to the already-released `0.3.2--0.3.3` update script.

=== Stop install and update scripts from leaking `search_path` and `client_min_messages`
After the transaction running `CREATE EXTENSION trunklet` or `ALTER EXTENSION trunklet UPDATE` ends, the caller's `search_path` and `client_min_messages` are unchanged. Within it, `search_path` is always unchanged; `client_min_messages` is too, except that a caller at `error` sees `warning` until the transaction ends when installing `0.2.0` or when updating from `0.2.0` or `0.2.1` (the `0.2.1--0.3.0` step).
The `0.2.0`, `0.2.1` and `0.3.3` install scripts and the `0.2.1--0.3.0` and `0.3.2--0.3.3` update scripts were edited only to change `SET` to `SET LOCAL`, including in the settings set-back where a script has one, and to add a comment that they were released with plain `SET`.

0.3.3
-----
=== Add `ignore_missing_functions` agument to `template_language__remove()`
This is necessary to support properly dropping a language that was installed as
part of an extension.

0.3.2
-----
=== Fix default version in trunklet.control

0.3.1
-----
=== Mark as stable

0.3.0
-----
== Add `template_language__remove()`
This makes it possible to remove an installed template language.
